WHAT: Extends simplify_expr to fold unsigned comparisons (Lt, Gt, Le, Ge)
using known-bits bounds, and eliminates the overflow check pattern
(x + c) < x when known-bits prove no overflow.

WHY: Fe's safe arithmetic generates redundant comparison+branch patterns
that evaluate to constants when the operand ranges are known. This pass
recognizes those patterns and folds them at the IR level.

GAS IMPACT: Minimal — only governance improved (-18 gas on delegate,
propose, vote). Most rosetta contracts use uaddo (checked add) rather
than the Add+Lt pattern this targets, so CheckedArithElim handles those
cases instead.

CODEGEN IMPACT: Test snapshots show the optimization correctly removes
patterns like `Lt v16 0.i256` (always false for unsigned). No opcode
count changes on rosetta contracts.

TEAM NOTES: This is a correct optimization but has limited practical
impact on Fe-generated code because the compiler prefers uaddo over
manual overflow checks. Worth keeping for correctness but don't expect
gas wins from this alone. The real overflow check elimination happens
in CheckedArithElim, which handles uaddo directly.
